---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { money } from "../../lib/format";
import { operator, privacyEmail, proPrice } from "../../lib/site";
---

<Legal
  locale="en"
  page="terms-of-service"
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The agreement between you and SubEye: what the app does, what Pro costs, what you own, and how either side ends it."
>
  <p>
    These terms are the agreement between you and SubEye. They are deliberately
    short, because the app is deliberately small.
  </p>

  <h2>Who you are agreeing with</h2>
  <p>
    SubEye is built and operated by {operator}, an individual based in Ukraine.
    Contact: <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What SubEye is</h2>
  <p>
    An iPhone app for recording subscriptions you already have and seeing what
    they cost. It is a record of what you tell it. It has no connection to your
    bank, it does not read your email, it cannot see your actual charges, and it
    cannot cancel anything on your behalf.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong
      >Every figure in the app is arithmetic on the numbers you entered.</strong
    > If a price you typed is wrong, or a merchant charges something different, or
    an exchange rate moves, the app will be wrong too. It is a tracker, not a statement,
    and it is not financial advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You need an account so your subscriptions survive a lost phone. You are
    responsible for keeping access to it — including the Google, GitHub or Apple
    account you sign in with, if you use one. One account is for one person.
  </p>
  <p>
    You must be 16 or older, and you must not use SubEye to break the law, to
    attack the service, or to attempt to reach data that is not yours.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data is yours</h2>
  <p>
    The subscriptions, notes and categories you enter belong to you. SubEye
    stores and processes them to run the service and for nothing else — see the
    <a href="/en/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>. No ownership of your
    content is claimed, and it is never sold.
  </p>

  <h2>Free and Pro</h2>
  <p>
    The free version is not a trial. Unlimited subscriptions, the whole
    dashboard, search and filters, every lifecycle action, a renewal reminder
    the day before, and multi-currency conversion are free and stay free.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>SubEye Pro is a single payment of {money(proPrice.usd, "usd")}</strong
    >, or the equivalent set for your App Store storefront — about {
      money(proPrice.uah, "uah", 0)
    } in Ukraine. It is not a subscription and it does not renew. It unlocks
    control over when reminders land, trial-ending and price-change tracking,
    and categories with the spend breakdown.
  </p>
  <p>
    Purchases are made through Apple, under Apple's terms. Refunds are handled
    by Apple, not by SubEye.
  </p>

  <h2>Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    Renewal reminders are scheduled on your device by iOS. If you deny
    notification permission, turn the device off, or force-quit the app for a
    long time, iOS may not deliver them. <strong
      >Do not rely on SubEye as your only defence against an unwanted
      renewal.</strong
    >
  </p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    SubEye is provided as it is, with no warranty of any kind. It is a small
    independent app: the service may be unavailable, may change, and may one day
    stop. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, but
    otherwise liability is limited to what you paid for SubEye Pro, if anything.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the service is going to be discontinued, reasonable notice will be given
    in the app so you can record your data first.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending it</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop at any time by deleting your account in Settings, which removes
    the account and every subscription in it. Access may be suspended or ended
    if these terms are broken in a way that harms the service or another person.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may change. The date at the top of this page will change with
    them, and a material change will be announced in the app before it takes
    effect. Continuing to use SubEye after that means you accept the new terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of Ukraine. If you are a consumer in the
    European Union or the United Kingdom, this does not remove the protections
    of your own country's law.
  </p>
</Legal>
